86152150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186152152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1031 "Approximating Volumes Using Upper Riemann Sums" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1033 2614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050800 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "67f29868-b7dd-582e-8c65-4c6fd95a9741" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186177526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186177527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186177528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186177530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186177526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177525 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "08b74d7c-dacb-56bb-92c4-735bc234302a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177526 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b728c5ad-8596-577f-b670-49ffcac95099" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177527 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177527 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177527 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c7bcbcc5-8a88-5065-9d5f-5f895561daaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177528 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177528 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177528 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "113bde06-2367-5118-9ad2-954102b4c31c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177530 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177530 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186177530 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36a7a1f5-d6d4-5cb0-8dda-4bde93389735" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179582 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9480" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179582 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2574b91a-6534-562b-b4dc-8d95fd19e169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179582 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179583 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179583 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179583 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f09771b-3e0d-567b-a39f-f877bff53372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179583 #edb/ref 1074 "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179585 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9484" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179585 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\nI. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\nII. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\nIII. $1 <     2  <    9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eff8c72f-429d-583a-aa22-f7786f09262a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179585 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179720 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179720 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179720 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179720 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/