 17592186049065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186523978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186524022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Partitions of the Real Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179723 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "2bc800b0-3901-5154-81ac-1ef853017320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1045 "Partitions of Intervals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179851 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bfa29f8b-fff6-5ca4-9fa7-be694c7b6715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186255954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd1432fb-079c-5b39-aa64-1524227d0162" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179974 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[0,3],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122849" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d3d4439-66c9-5ffc-a015-2454a6d340fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179975 #edb/ref 1074 "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186177525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,8]?$\n\nI. $1<2<4<8$\n\nII. $\\{1,3,4,8\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{2,4,8\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ab45c0e-0c7c-5664-9875-fc74cbb23147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179976 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,8].$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[1,8]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1061 22785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef5d4a8f-ff27-5806-af27-4b7ffb16f3c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180381 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1061 35481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "adc61151-e0b6-5426-832a-962b7f89c76e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180461 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1061 35489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "589bd944-74be-586b-b8aa-de1f404e6b97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180462 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1061 35493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "866321d3-59e7-5859-b4e4-2adecd40dfc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180464 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1061 35494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "58b0b85b-9601-5c14-a9f6-12ded310b31e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180465 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1064 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nFor example, given the interval $[0,6],$ one possible partition is \n\n$$\n0 < 2 < 5 < 6.\n$$\n\nWe can express this partition using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{0,2,5,6\\}.\n$$\n\nNote that this partition breaks up the interval $[0,6]$ into the union of the following subintervals:\n\n$$\n[0,2] \\cup [2,5] \\cup [5,6]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1065 3874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "874ce92b-031e-55f5-92e4-5883ab9f029a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180675 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have the partition $P=\\{0,2,5,6\\}$ of the interval $[a,b]=[0,6].$ Then, we have\n\n$$\na=\\underbrace{0}_{\\large x_0}   <   \\underbrace{2}_{\\large x_1}   <  \\underbrace{5}_{\\large x_2} <  \\underbrace{6}_{\\large x_3} =b.\n$$\n\nThis partition breaks up the interval $[0,6]$ into the union of the following subintervals:\n\n$$\n[0,2] \\cup [2,5] \\cup [5,6]\n$$\n\nThe length of the $i$th subinterval, denoted $\\Delta x_i,$ is simply the difference of the endpoints: \n\n- The length of the first interval $[0,2],$ denoted $\\Delta x_1,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{1} & ={x}_{1}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The length of the second interval $[2,5],$ denoted $\\Delta x_2,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{2} & ={x}_{2}-{x}_{1} \\\\  & =5-2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The length of the third interval $[5,6],$ denoted $\\Delta x_3,$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{x}_{3} & ={x}_{3}-{x}_{2} \\\\  & =6-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}Δ{x}_{i} & =Δ{x}_{1}+Δ{x}_{2}+Δ{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2+3+1 \\\\  & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is just the length of the interval $[0, 6].$\n\n**Note:** In general, for any partition $P=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_m\\}$ of an interval $[a,b],$ the sum \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i\n$$\n\n is just the length of the interval $[a, b],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =Δ{x}_{1}+Δ{x}_{2}+Δ{x}_{3}+⋯+Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1065 5779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "714f6267-47f5-5ba8-a3e7-3b7ef319e601" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180706 #edb/ref 1067 "Sums Over Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253841 #edb/ref 1080 "28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253841 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253841 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "141db895-bbc5-5054-af56-41c9ff81d0a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253892 #edb/ref 1080 "-24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253892 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253892 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a21aab7-fc2e-549f-aab8-41f5bccb2b74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254042 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254042 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254042 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29baeff2-fc72-53fa-9693-cdc59cdd0aba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254221 #edb/ref 1080 "28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254221 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254221 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3fdb0422-e00a-5e11-8104-48d5cd25b697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254361 #edb/ref 1080 "36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254361 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254361 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4f652284-78d1-58c0-9b15-97c5c58fc918" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254371 #edb/ref 1080 "-28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254371 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254371 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "507bca0f-38a3-53f7-b541-4c90fdccc251" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254406 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254406 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254406 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5452a419-f554-5118-a23f-5cda88d07a6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254502 #edb/ref 1080 "21" #edb/ref 1759218