86045436] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462804 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-3,7]?$\n- **I.** ${-3,-5,1,2,6}$\n- **II.** ${-3,0,3,7,8}$\n- **III.** ${-3,-2,1,3,4,7}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bede805a-096d-538b-aca7-d4841b6beb80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256749 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=7.$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-3,7]$ since $8$ does not belong to $[-3,7].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[-3,7].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462805 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462806 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186462807 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[0,4]?$\n- **I.** $0<0.5<1.5<2.5<4<4.5$\n- **II.** ${0,1,2,3.9}$\n- **III.** $0<0.1<1.5<2.5<4$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8952dce8-c604-5674-b4ed-f948b3d55e92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256750 #edb/ref 1074 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since $4.5$ does not belong to $[0,4].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[0,4]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=4.$\n\n- Statement III is  a partition of  $[0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122977" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[2,10].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "108d22ab-96a8-5eeb-96fd-0dcc96561441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256761 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the factor $(-4)$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}-4Δ{x}_{i}=-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,10],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=(-4)\\cdot 8=-32.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[4,9].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99e23ff1-d646-54b7-8668-22a06e7d8b04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256762 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we take the factor $7$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}7Δ{z}_{k}=7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,9],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+({z}_{3}-{z}_{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}}-{z}_{0})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{z}_{3}}-\\cancel{{z}_{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}+{z}_{q} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}-{z}_{0} \\\\  & =9-4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n7{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}Δ{z}_{k}=7\\cdot 5=35.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186256241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $P=\\{{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,4].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e65ff59b-de1e-50f4-9c3d-679e5004d29d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256768 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=(-2)\\cdot 12=-24.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186462097 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26715d5c-8967-5870-a32d-f0e7de04504e" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462098 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cffe34d1-2420-5409-9740-ce2cb5bd06e5" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462099 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462099 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5500db0b-5028-5ca1-9101-be045fa07fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462100 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462100 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186462100 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f59f0c27-693f-5b74-9c2c-1f